{"context":"Existing code-context execution items are marked done, but cmd/code_context.go remains a stub. ADR-034 defines deterministic code graph as derived Runtime cache and rejects RAG/vector search as canonical or primary path.","decision":"Define code_context contract with two orthogonal axes: depth controls relationship scope (local, dependency, engineering), default dependency; level controls code-context composition as integer 0..3, default 1. L0 is symbol signature and bounded slice; L1 adds imports and one-hop refs; L2 adds related test refs; L3 adds lazy config refs. CLI exposes --level and retains --depth for relationship scope. MCP exposes matching level and depth fields through direct code_context tool backed by shared core logic. Output remains deterministic, bounded, and provenance-aware. RAG is deferred follow-up/plugin research: never canonical, never primary graph source, never enters CKO, snapshot, or canonical cache; optional enrichment must be explicitly marked and must not alter deterministic results.","consequences":"One semantic model prevents depth/level confusion and enables token-cost control. Defaults preserve current stub intent. Direct MCP wiring avoids CLI proxy coupling. MVP excludes vector dependency and full call graph; unsupported symbols/languages use bounded deterministic fallback or explicit low-confidence refs per implementation design. Existing eka context/get and CKO/RSF contracts remain unchanged.","alternativesConsidered":"Alias --level to --depth rejected because they represent different axes. RAG as primary rejected by ADR-034 due to non-determinism, model coupling, re-index cost, and hallucination risk. CLI proxy rejected as default MCP path due to latency and error coupling."}